{"orgCode":"0989","name":"California Educational Facilities Authority","agencyCode":"0010","agencyName":"Legislative, Judicial, and Executive","description":"The California Educational Facilities Authority (CEFA) provides students with better access and broader opportunities in higher education by providing qualified private non-profit higher education institutions with the assistance needed to reduce their capital costs of financing academic related facilities through a tax-exempt revenue bond program.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":79,"cy":79,"by":79},"positions":{"py":3,"cy":4,"by":4},"excluded":{"nongovernmental":{"py":721,"cy":1022,"by":1023}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/0010/0989","kind":"department","name":"California Educational Facilities Authority","code":"0989","amounts":{"py":79,"cy":79,"by":79},"positions":{"py":3,"cy":4,"by":4},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":79,"cy":79,"by":79}},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0989/0955","kind":"program","name":"College Access Tax Credit Program","code":"0955","amounts":{"py":79,"cy":79,"by":79},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":79,"cy":79,"by":79}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"description":"0955 - COLLEGE ACCESS TAX CREDIT FUND\n\nThe College Access Tax Credit Fund (Fund) provides a 50% tax credit to taxpayers and businesses who make a contribution to the College Access Tax Credit Fund to support California Community College transfer students attending partnered Historically Black Colleges and Universities (HBCU) and who intend to return to California following the completion of their studies through the Cal-HBCU Transfer Grant Program administered through the California Student Aid Commission. The tax credit can be used to offset or reduce the taxpayer's taxes.\n\nCEFA is required to allocate and certify up to $500 million in tax credits through taxable year 2027.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":79,"cy":79,"by":79}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0989/0955/f3263","kind":"fund","name